  <h2 id="case">One exchanger tube. Three different questions.</h2>
  <p>A straight tube stands in for one member of a tube-bundle heat exchanger. First ask what pressure does to it. Then ask how it expands when heated. Finally ask what happens if the tube sheets prevent that axial expansion. These are separate verification cases, not a combined pressure-and-temperature design analysis.</p>
  <svg class="tube-diagram" viewBox="0 0 680 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="tube-title tube-desc">
    <title id="tube-title">Idealized heat exchanger tube and separate axial thermal restraints</title><desc id="tube-desc">Schematic, not a CAD model or computed field. A 1 metre straight tube has a 10 millimetre bore radius and 1 millimetre wall. Thermal cases compare a sliding end with axial restraint at both ends.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="5" refY="3.5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L7 3.5L0 7" fill="#76ddd7"/></marker></defs>
    <rect width="680" height="240" rx="14" fill="#142127"/>
    <g fill="#d8e8ec" font-family="system-ui,sans-serif"><text x="28" y="30" font-size="15">Synthetic tube · schematic, not a solver field</text>
    <path d="M98 73H560V117H98Z" fill="#32474f" stroke="#a9bec5"/><path d="M98 84H560V106H98Z" fill="#142127" stroke="#a9bec5"/>
    <path d="M124 95H530" stroke="#76ddd7" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><text x="257" y="69" font-size="14">Pressure-only: 2 MPa gauge inside</text>
    <path d="M98 139H560" stroke="#76ddd7" marker-start="url(#arrow)" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><text x="298" y="162" font-size="14">L = 1 m</text>
