    <label>Length (m)<input name="length" type="number" min="0.05" max="5" step="0.05" value="1" required /></label>
    <label>Elastic modulus (GPa)<input name="modulus" type="number" min="1" max="500" step="1" value="190" required /></label>
    <label>Expansion coefficient (10⁻⁶/K)<input name="alpha" type="number" min="0" max="50" step="0.5" value="16" required /></label>
    <label>Temperature rise (K)<input name="temperature" type="number" min="0" max="200" step="1" value="80" required /></label>
    <button type="submit">Recalculate analytical predictions</button>
  </form>
  <output id="hx-proof-output" aria-live="polite" class="calc-output">Bore hoop stress: 21.048 MPa · free extension: 1.280 mm · axial restrained stress: −243.200 MPa · reaction magnitude: 16.045 kN.</output>
  <p class="small-note">ν = 0.30; outside gauge pressure = 0; uniform constant properties. No allowable stress, buckling check, material certification, combined-load model, or engineering PASS is inferred from these numbers.</p>
  <h2>What would make this an exchanger FEA qualification?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Freeze the real question, geometry, material data, pressure loads, temperatures, restraints, outputs, and acceptance criteria before solving.</li>
    <li>Use the relevant conventional solver. Retain native fields, mesh, element formulation, reactions, warnings, and input decks.</li>
    <li>Check pressure and reaction equilibrium, thermoelastic assumptions, mesh sensitivity, and relevant local stresses away from artificial singularities.</li>
    <li>Investigate tube-sheet contact, joints, thermal gradients, yielding, buckling, fatigue, and mapped-fluid loads where physically applicable.</li>
    <li>Separate numerical verification, physical validation, code compliance, and the engineer's release authority. Never promote an LLM explanation into observed solver evidence.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Existing retained conventional examples remain available in <a href="/software/aero/current/?case=fea-tube-20260912">Aero's pressure-tube case</a>, <a href="/software/aero/current/?case=fea-thermal-free-20260912">free thermal case</a>, and <a href="/software/aero/current/?case=fea-thermal-fixed-20260912">restrained thermal case</a>. They have their own inputs and dispositions; these new numbers do not rescore them.</p>
